{"seq":14,"trial_id":"shared-brain-access-2026-11/claude-code-opus-gbrain-told-open-mu-v031-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-22T13:26:20.073Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"429a31d7ac721b6e2ea9e480ebf48866cc6f7ca4394f176e8cb739924d804487","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","text":"Hi Dana. I went through all six of Moss's notes. Two ticket numbers on Quarrendon Freight Lines turn up:\n\n• *#PD-4492*, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (5 Oct 2025). Thea Ramaswell logged it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers on the 04:00 shift at Dock Doors 14–18 in Eau Claire weren't getting SMS bay assignments at the gatehouse kiosk. Support patched the SMS gateway routing at 19:30 that day, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct 04:00 shift cleared the gate. The same note also has an action item to archive the Eau Claire kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n• *#4419*, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet\" (undated). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners at Door 14 weren't reading trailer tags on third shift. The note says it went to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing.\n\nMoss's 14 Sep 2025 pipeline digest and 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in both mention QFL but don't give a ticket number. The two Central notes don't cover QFL.\n\nBefore #4419 goes in the weekly notes: Marcus's own Q2 expansion wrap (14 Jul 2025, not a Moss note) uses #4419 for something else, \"Gate 3 printer lag,\" a BOL printout delay that support had patched. So the same number has two different descriptions, and I can't tell from the notes which one is right. It's probably worth checking with Marcus or support."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
